          "title": "The arithmetic test \u2014 categorical vs numerical",
          "lede": "One question separates the two types: does arithmetic on these values mean anything?",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_data_shape_and_types.r02.b01",
              "role": "definition",
              "text": "Ask yourself: would adding or subtracting two values from this column produce a meaningful result? For delivery_min, yes \u2014 41 minutes minus 32 minutes is 9 minutes, a real difference. For city, no \u2014 'Lagos' minus 'Abuja' means nothing. For zone_code, no \u2014 102 minus 101 is not a meaningful distance between zones. delivery_min is numerical; city and zone_code are categorical.",
